  ('30b06de3-0cc0-4863-8746-b36bdb5656a0', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '684fc31b-012f-4f53-b7ae-e5aa863b3450', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$On Christmas Eve, the entire town was filled with excitement and joy. Preparations were in full swing. Joy, a five-year-old boy, was the happiest among them. He lived with his old grandfather, Joseph. Joy had been orphaned as a baby and raised by Joseph ever since. Joy had seen his grandfather work in the fields and how he had always found ways to bring happiness and wisdom to his grandson’s life. Each day after returning from the fields, despite his fatigue, he spends time with Joy, teaching him about kindness, patience and love. Joy noticed how hard his Grandpa worked and how little he complained. Why do you think Joy’s Grandpa worked so hard? This beautiful story teaches us the value of selflessness and thoughtfulness in a heartwarming way. Let’s ! M— This year's winter was harsher and it rained occasionally. Joy saw how Joseph would come home shivering, his coat drenched with rain. English-8 @$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-30T06-17-51-467Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 25, NULL),
